#: action.py:HELP_HTML
#, python-brace-format
msgid "<h3>Recommended workflow</h3><ol><li><b>Run Integrity Analysis</b> and read the report.</li><li>Fix the real problems (missing files, damaged folders...). The affected books are marked so you can find them.</li><li>For the issues that are intentional (for example, empty records you keep on purpose), select those books and use <b>Exclusions &gt; Exclude selected books</b>, or use <b>Exclude every issue in the last report</b> to add them all at once.</li><li>Run the analysis again: the report now shows only the issues that still need attention.</li></ol><h3>Menu options</h3><p><b>Run Integrity Analysis</b>: scans every book of the current library. The progress window lets you cancel; in that case the report is partial.</p><p><b>View Last Integrity Report</b>: shows the last report again, grouped by book. Each issue shows its check type in brackets: [no_formats], [formats], [folder], [opf], [cover] or [io].</p><p><b>Export Report to .txt</b>: saves the report to a text file.</p><p><b>Mark problematic books</b>: marks the books of the last report with the text <i>{mark}</i> and shows them. You can also find them by typing <code>marked:\"={mark}\"</code> in the search bar.</p><p><b>Show marked problematic books</b>: shows only the marked books again. Clear the search bar to see the whole library.</p><p><b>Clear integrity marks</b>: removes only the marks added by this plugin.</p><h3>Exclusions submenu</h3><p><b>Exclude selected books</b>: select books first. You choose which checks to ignore for them:</p><ul><li><i>All checks</i>: the book is skipped entirely.</li><li><i>Book without formats (empty record)</i>: for records that only hold metadata.</li><li><i>Missing or empty format files</i>, <i>Missing book folder</i>, <i>Missing or empty metadata.opf</i>, <i>Missing cover.jpg</i>.</li></ul><p>If the books appear in the last report, the checks they failed are already ticked.</p><p><b>Exclude every issue in the last report</b>: adds all the books of the report, each one only with the checks it failed. If a new, different problem appears later in one of them, it will still be reported.</p><p><b>Remove selected books from exclusions</b>: those books will be checked again.</p><p><b>Show excluded books in the library</b>: filters the library to the excluded books.</p><p><b>Open exclusions file</b>: opens the JSON with your editor. Besides the books, you can fill the <code>excluded_tags</code> list: any book with one of those tags is skipped entirely.</p><p><b>Import / Export exclusions</b>: merge another JSON into yours, or save a copy (backup or another computer). Books are identified by their uuid, so exclusions keep working even if the id changes.</p><h3>Configure Plugin</h3><p>Turn each check on or off. If you never want empty records to be reported, uncheck <i>Report books without any format</i>. You can also turn off automatic marking and choose where the exclusions file is stored.</p>"
msgstr ""


